From a9a829c2e3990da7b69ef8c68526a8807d3c76cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Isaac Duarte <31712685+Isaac-Duarte@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:19:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] PCI: apple: qualify the J714s for suspend-to-idle over
 the adopted N1 link

The adopted-link check admits the J716c, the K114c and the K116s. The
J714s (MacBook Pro 14", M5 Pro) has the same T6050 host as the K116s,
with the N1 on port 0, and every s2idle there failed in the noirq
suspend:

  pcie-apple 1cb0000000.pcie: PM: dpm_run_callback(): apple_pcie_suspend_noirq returns -16
  pcie-apple 1cb0000000.pcie: PM: failed to suspend noirq: error -16

Like the K116s, the J714s has its SD card reader (a GL9755) on port 1,
which the boot loader leaves down and Linux trains itself. The previous
commit lets the devices below such a port leave D0 over s2idle, which
the check needs on this board too.

Add the J714s to the list. For a clean wake it also needs the PMP's
power domains kept on ("arm64: dts: apple: t6050: keep the PMP's power
domains on"), and for the Type-C ports to work after the wake, the ATC
usb-aon domains kept on ("arm64: dts: apple: t6050: keep the ATC usb-aon
power domains on").

Signed-off-by: Isaac Duarte <31712685+Isaac-Duarte@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
index 439daa464e2b..cf8ad34c9b7e 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
@@ -6569,13 +6569,15 @@ static int apple_pcie_check_adopted_s2idle(struct apple_pcie *pcie)
 	int error = 0;
 
 	/*
-	 * Qualified on the J716c, the K114c and the K116s. The K116s is the
-	 * J716c's OLED sibling: the same T6050 host, the N1 on port 0. Other
-	 * adopted platforms and deeper sleep remain unqualified.
+	 * Qualified on the J716c, the K114c, the K116s and the J714s: the same
+	 * T6050 host with the N1 adopted on port 0. The K116s and the J714s
+	 * (16- and 14-inch M5 Pro) also have a kernel-trained SD reader port.
+	 * Other adopted platforms and deeper sleep remain unqualified.
 	 */
 	if (!(of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j716c") ||
 	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,k114c") ||
-	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,k116s")) || !pm_suspend_no_platform())
+	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,k116s") ||
+	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j714s")) || !pm_suspend_no_platform())
 		return -EBUSY;
 
 	if (!(readl(pcie->base + CORE_RC_CTL) & CORE_RC_CTL_RUN) ||
